sentences containing \"reasoning\" and \"snowball\", then embed them into report JSON built in code. That's programmatic but the content is real text.\n\nRisk: extracted sentence might not support both categories fully. Categories: one sentence listing reasoning, acting, interacting. Let me search for pattern. I'll write code: extract page 4 text flattened, find all sentences, pick sentence containing \"reasoning\" and \"acting\" and \"interacting\". Similarly page 5 for \"Google Scholar\" and \"snowballing\" sentence (maybe picks \"We used Google Scholar ... snowballing ...\").\n\nThen build report JSON in Python, write via write_file (need expected_hash of report.json = ca3d16... from registered full read). Then run pytest, update plan, final_answer.\n\nAlso need write_note calls? Notes already exist per feedback (5 notes present). Good.\n\nAlso overview: total overview text (200-600 chars) and per-section summary/application in Chinese — I write these as literals.\n\nEvidence quotes for other sections: I have from delivered evidence:\n- reasoning self_consistency: p.10 quote \"A popular approach is Self Consistency [Wang et al., 2022]. Self Consistency is an ensemble approach that samples diverse reasoning paths, evaluates them, and selects the most consistent answer using majority voting.\" Good (continuous, from p.10 evidence text).\n- ToT: p.13 \"The paper describes both a breadth-first and a depth-first controller.\" Combined with prior sentence: \"When one reasoning path has been traversed, the search backtracks, and tries an alternative. The paper describes both a breadth-first and a depth-first controller.\" Continuous in evidence text? Text: \"When one reasoning path\\nhas been traversed, the search backtracks, and tries an alternative. The paper describes both a breadth-first and a\\ndepth-first controller.\" Yes continuous. Quote: \"The paper describes both a breadth-first and a depth-first controller.\" — 20+ chars, supports both? It mentions both cont